DESCRIPTION:Slater Museum is pleased to present\, "Alexey von Schlippe: Ex
 pressions of Mind and Soul\," opening on July 29! This ongoing exhibition 
 will be the newest addition to the museum's permanent galleries\, showcasi
 ng the works of renowned educator and artist\, Alexey von Schlippe. Von Sc
 hlippe lived in Norwich for many years\, teaching at the Norwich Art Schoo
 l in the 1950s and '60s before being appointed as a Professor at the Unive
 rsity of Connecticut. The Alexey von Schlippe Gallery of Art at UConn Aver
 y Point was named in his honor after his passing in 1988.\n\nSource: https
 ://ctvisit.com/events/alexey-von-schlippe-expressions-mind-and-soul
