BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Closing the Ring: George Washington’s War in the North\, 1778-17
 81
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260916
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260917
DTSTAMP:20260915T152704Z
UID:7bb5f03b2dd529b26d7913f1c5fd@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:In the fall of 1778\, Washington was occupied with ascertainin
 g British intentions through his spy network in New York City. Join teache
 r & historian Jeffrey Denman for a book talk exploring Washington’s nort
 hern campaigns after 1778\, which are often overlooked but demonstrate Was
 hington’s great skill in strategy\, logistics\, and diplomacy. Discover 
 the impact of the raids of New Haven\, Fairfield\, and Norwalk in 1779 and
  the final years of the Revolutionary War. Book sale & signing to follow. 
 Members: $5\; Non-Members: $10.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/clos
 ing-ring-george-washingtons-war-north-1778-1781
LOCATION:Fairfield Museum & History Center\, 370 Beach Rd\, Fairfield\, CT
 \, 06824\, Fairfield CT\, 06824
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/closing-ring-george-washingtons-war-north-1
 778-1781
END:VEVENT
