DTSTAMP:20260915T152704Z
UID:18def16c2b7eba3b1f29f0b6ce37@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Located at the mouth of the Thames River\, Fort Trumbull is si
 tauted perfectly to catch migrating shorebirds on their way south. The exp
 ansive lawns\, sandy flats\, and rocky islands attract a variety of specie
 s\, while the river and sound are home to gulls and waterfowl. The walk wi
 ll be approximately .5-.75 miles on level grassy\, paved\, and dirt terrai
 n. Exposure to sun\, heat/cold\, and wind possible depending on weather. P
 ortable toilets on site.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/shorebird-w
 alk-3
LOCATION:Fort Trumbull State Park\, 90 Walbach Street\, New London CT\, 06
 320
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/shorebird-walk-3
END:VEVENT
